B.a2_=s(["First Lady IAS Officer: Indra Mallo Tana.","First Male IAS Officer: Jomin Tayeng.","First MP from Arunachal: Chow Khamoon Gohain Namshum (1952).","First Mountaineer to summit Mt. Everest: Tapi Mra.","First Woman to scale Mt. Everest: Tine Mena (9 May 2011, Echali, Upper Dibang Valley).","World Record Everest Ascents: Anshu Jamsenpa (fastest double ascent within 5 days by a woman).","First Nyishi Woman to scale Everest: Kabak Yano (May 2024).",'First Film in Arunachalee (Sherdukpen) language: "Crossing Bridges" directed by Sange Dorjee Thangdok (Won Rajat Kamal in 61st National Film Awards 2013).',"First Daily Newspaper: Echo of Arunachal.",'First Arunachalee to receive Sahitya Akademi Award: Yeshe Dorjee Thongchi (for "Mouna Onth Mukher Hirdoy" in 2005).',"Largest Monastery: Tawang Monastery (400 years old, largest in India, 2nd largest in the world after Potala Palace)."],t.s)
